# Exam Proctor — System Design Reference

Before writing or modifying code in this project, read:

- **[docs/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md](../../docs/SYSTEM_DESIGN.md)** — architecture, models, APIs, confirmed decisions
- **[docs/PLAN.md](../../docs/PLAN.md)** — UI conventions (Flaticon icons, no emojis, monochromatic text hierarchy), portal navigation plan

That document is the single source of truth for:

- Architecture, data flows, and project layout
- Database models and relationships
- API endpoints and WebSocket channels
- ML/proctoring background processing (Celery, YOLOv5, face match)
- Confirmed design decisions (session auth, exam codes, strict lockdown, etc.)
- **Question Bank Builder UI**, teacher exam workflow, and admin approval/freeze/add-time controls (§2.1–§2.2)
- **Unified portal navigation**: single sidebar at `templates/includes/portal_sidebar.html` with `portal_nav` active key (see `.cursor/rules/confirm-todo-list.mdc`)
- **UI iconography**: no emojis — use Flaticon icons per `docs/PLAN.md`
- **UI typography**: monochromatic hierarchy — no colored alert text; use weight + neutral notice cards per `docs/PLAN.md`
- Implementation phase checklist

When implementing a feature, align with the confirmed decisions in section 0 of SYSTEM_DESIGN.md. Do not introduce JWT auth, open exam access, or external ID database lookups unless the design doc is updated first.
